 "blocks": [
  {
   "t": "figure",
   "html": "<img src=\"@img:images/detexpert-logosml_aok62ui8.png\" alt=\"crawfords metal detectors\" title=\"paul cee minelab\" width=\"245\" height=\"360\">"
  },
  {
   "t": "h2",
   "html": "Minelab Equinox 4 tone settings"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "After reading a comment on Pauls Youtube channel, he mentioned to somebody about"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Setting up a 4 Tone Detecting method.. A Reply came about that the <a href=\"@minelab-equinox/\" data-kind=\"internal\">Equinox 800</a> has only 2 tones, 3 tones, 5 tones and 50 tones."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "<em> So where does the 4 tones come from? The Answer is very simple.</em>"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "<a href=\"@crawfords-metal-detectors/\" data-kind=\"internal\"><img src=\"@img:images/4-tones.jpg\" alt=\"equinox tone settings\" title=\"Equinox 800 settings 4 tones\" width=\"223\" height=\"396\"></a>"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Its all to do with how you set the Tones in the Equinox settings."
  },
  {
   "t": "h3",
   "html": "Each Tones break has a selectable tone right?",
   "inferred": true
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "So if you have a 5 tone setting and have the TONE BREAKS set as to where you require them if you have adjusted them as a previous post"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "all you then have to do is adjust one of the TONE PITCHES to the same Value as a Tone pitch next to it and hey presto you have the 4 TONES."
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Hope this has cleared up any confusion, if you have found it useful please leave a comment below"
  },
  {
   "t": "p",
   "html": "Thanks DW.."
  }
 ],
